{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261023T014653Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "51888f116f5b083740bce796", "title": "Turning Database Grading into RL Rewards: Post-Training Agents with ThinkingBox", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/microsoft/thinkingbox-training", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-22T22:24:34+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.9775, "worthiness_confidence": 0.93, "final_score": 0.9775, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 26885, "delivered": true, "summary": "Microsoft and Hugging Face built ThinkingBox-Training, which converts database state checks into RL rewards for agent post-training. Training Qwen3.8-27B with GRPO on 187 offline-selected tasks for 50 steps improved pass@1 from 51.70% to 60.78%, and tasks passing all 20 attempts jumped from 38 to 107. The key insight: offline policy-relative difficulty selection—using Beta posteriors from base-model probes to identify tasks with mixed success rates—maximizes GRPO's learning signal by avoiding always-solved or unsolvable tasks. This approach reduces cost per dependable task by 67% while maintaining out-of-distribution generalization to the 507-task ThinkingBox-Bench.", "jev_ms": 173.2, "jev_input_tokens": 7922, "jev_cost": 0.000332724, "llm_ms": 4457.1, "llm_cost": 0.008715, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261023T014653Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "67297d2df9a3d7f196c35fa6", "title": "OlmoEarth v1.3: State-of-the-art embeddings for the whole planet", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/allenai/olmoearth-v1-3", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-22T16:11:31+00:00", "is_ai": 0.98, "worthiness": 0.7775, "worthiness_confidence": 0.91, "final_score": 0.7775, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 7804, "delivered": true, "summary": "Allen AI released OlmoEarth v1.3, a satellite embedding model producing 128-dimensional vectors for every 10-meter pixel on Earth using Sentinel-1, Sentinel-2, and Landsat time series data. The model outperforms AlphaEarth Foundations and Tessera v2 on 20 of 27 evaluations while requiring 53% less compute than v1.2. Precomputed global embeddings enable lightweight downstream tasks like crop classification and change detection without GPU access or fine-tuning. An interactive browser-based explorer lets users find similar locations and train classifiers directly on embeddings. This shifts satellite analysis from expensive per-task fine-tuning to efficient embedding reuse, democratizing planetary-scale monitoring.", "jev_ms": 242.3, "jev_input_tokens": 2493, "jev_cost": 0.000104706, "llm_ms": 3411.1, "llm_cost": 0.003026, "errors": []}
